From: minmax <minmax@archempc>
Date: Sun, 11 May 2026
Subject: [PATCH] net: macb: disable flow control advertisement for rp1-gem

Remove MAC_ASYM_PAUSE from mac_capabilities so the PHY does not
advertise asymmetric pause frames during autonegotiation. This
prevents TX pause frames from being negotiated on Raspberry Pi 5
(raspberrypi,rp1-gem), which was causing interference with network
performance testing.

Tested on: Raspberry Pi 5 (BCM2712), kernel 6.12.87-v8-16k-rpi-2712
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
index 728f55265..ad4bf4e69 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
@@ -980,7 +980,7 @@ static int macb_mii_probe(struct net_device *dev)
 		bp->phylink_config.get_fixed_state = macb_get_pcs_fixed_state;
 	}

-	bp->phylink_config.mac_capabilities = MAC_ASYM_PAUSE |
+	bp->phylink_config.mac_capabilities =
 		MAC_10 | MAC_100;

 	__set_bit(PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_MII,
--
2.43.0
